<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Third Taifa of Málaga</h1><p class="st-meta">1145 CE – 1153 CE (approx.) · capital Málaga</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Málaga under its qadi Ibn Hassun, who ruled the city independently after the Almoravid collapse until the Almohads forced him out.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1145, as Andalusi cities expelled their Almoravid garrisons, the people of Málaga accepted the authority of their qadi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-al-hakam-ibn-hassun">Abu al-Hakam ibn Hassun</a>, a member of a local family of jurists.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qadi">qadis</a> of the second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> period, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-al-hakam-ibn-hassun">Ibn Hassun</a> ruled on the strength of his religious office and local support. He governed a prosperous port, but had little military power and faced pressure from Almoravid loyalists, from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-jaen">Taifa of Jaén</a> and from the advancing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1153 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> took Málaga, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-al-hakam-ibn-hassun">Ibn Hassun</a> is reported to have killed himself rather than be captured. The city remained under Almohad and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasrid-dynasty">Nasrid</a> rule until 1487.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1145 CE – 1153 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.49%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1145 CE – 1153 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Málaga</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abu al-Hakam ibn Hassun</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Málaga of Ibn Hassun</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1149&amp;focus=third-taifa-of-malaga" aria-label="Third Taifa of Málaga on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4569 854 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Third Taifa of Málaga lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4889 1110L4799 1289M4889 1110L4794 1282"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4799 1289h0M4794 1282h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4889 1110h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4889 1110h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Málaga. <a href="/atlas?year=1149&amp;focus=third-taifa-of-malaga">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
